// transientSourceYieldWake (case_on): the schedule case. Same arm `u` as
// case_off plus a single source on the same free node, ramping 0 -> 2e-6 m3/s
// over [1.2, 1.4] s (steps 600..700), holding, then ramping back to 0 over
// [2.0, 2.2] s (steps 1000..1100). Both ramps sit inside the drain's sealed
// window [500, 1350], so the source is the only thing that can move the node
// during the hold.
//
// New kernel hook: `sources{ inj { node F; schedule { openRate 2e-6; close {
// start 1.2; end 1.4; } open { start 2.0; end 2.2; } } } }`. The schedule
// shares the ramp shape with valveClose / valveOpen on a pipe; the source
// rate is evaluated at the same implicit new time level t + dt as the valve
// K. A source without a schedule{} is constant (5.52..5.60 behaviour), and
// a `rate` key can be supplied instead for the constant-rate form; this file
// exercises only the schedule form, so the case_off file above is the
// control (no sources block at all).
//
// The row per arm is unchanged. The node balance picks up one more `+ Q_inj`
// term in sumIn, and the liquid inventory picks up `dt * Q_inj` in commitStep.
// Both follow the ramp continuously, so the Newton residual at each step
// still sees a smooth sumIn.
//
// What the schedule is predicted to buy: with case_off the sealed-window
// ceiling is the wall's own release pressure pA - threshold = 22000 Pa (the
// wall flows, the wall holds the ceiling). With case_on the source is added
// on top of the wall's flow, so the node climbs past 22000 during the hold
// and the wall is asked to re-latch; when the source ramps off the node
// falls back to 22000 and the wall wakes again. The threshold and the
// release pressure are schedule-blind, so the two files share the same two
// integers (22000 Pa / 8000 Pa) and differ only in the STEP each latch fires.

fluid
{
    rho 850; mu 0.1;
}

nodes
{
    A { fixedPressure 3.0e4; }
    B { fixedPressure 2.0e4; }
    F { volume 0.1; bulkModulus 1.0e8; pressure 2.7e4; }
}

pipes
{
    Sa { from A; to F; length 20; diameter 0.02;
         flowIndex 0.5; consistency 1.0; yieldStress 2.0; }
    Da { from F; to B; length 20; diameter 0.02; valve 0;
         valveClose { start 0.8; end 1.0; closedK 1.0e8; }
         valveOpen  { start 2.5; end 2.7; } }
}

sources
{
    inj
    {
        node F;
        schedule
        {
            openRate 2.0e-6;
            close { start 1.2; end 1.4; }
            open  { start 2.0; end 2.2; }
        }
    }
}

time
{
    dt 0.002;
    endTime 4.0;
    reportEvery 1;
}
